# The brief forbids submitting dataset downloads or large checkpoints. What
# the report is built from -- results, figures, the subset manifest and the
# configuration -- is committed; the artifacts they were derived from are not.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.DS_Store

# The MNIST download. The 10,000-image subset is rebuilt by
# scripts/build_mnist_subset.py from the committed manifest, at the same
# seed, so the images themselves do not need to be in the repository.
data/MNIST/
data/*.gz
!data/subset_manifest.json

# Build intermediate for the PDF.
report/*.html

# Results, figures and the generated report are written by every run,
# including the smoke and scouting runs used while developing. A report
# built from a scouting run reads exactly like one built from the real
# thing, so these are ignored by default and the genuine set is added
# deliberately with `git add -f results/ plots/ report/` once both final
# runs complete. A number enters the repository as a decision.
results/*.json
results/*.csv
results/*.pt
plots/*.png
report/*.md
report/*.pdf

# Model weights. Small for this architecture, but the brief asks that
# checkpoints not be submitted; the run is cheap enough to reproduce.
checkpoints/
*.pt
!results/fixed_noise.pt

# The executed notebook is committed deliberately once src/ is final,
# for the same reason as the report: an executed notebook from a smoke
# run is indistinguishable from the real one at a glance.
GAN_MNIST.ipynb
